    "id": 5,
    "date": "2019-09-23T14:01:29+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Some basic rules for living:\n\nIt may sound simple, but it's a natural law ... accidents and other bad things happen to us when we're in the wrong place at the wrong time.\n\nAs such, it's important when we leave a place, or embark upon any task or journey, however trival, that we pause and reflect, and that we start out in peace and in the right mind.\n\nWe don't want to hurt ourselves or have accidents; lose things, forget things or leave things behind; drop things, break things or force things.\n\nWe don't want things stolen from us.\n\nBe alert, awake and aware.\n\nBe gentle, relaxed and at peace.\n\nAlways act with forethought and clear intent.\n\nAlways be on guard and aware of who is watching.\n\nThe world can be a dangerous place.\n\nBe vilgilant.",
    "media": null
